cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset or code, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "CZ-Dataset-Doe: steady CFD reference dataset of Czochralski silicon-melt flow over a three-parameter design of experiments"
authors:
  - given-names: Bertwin
    family-names: Kurisinkal Shine
    affiliation: Chemnitz University of Technology
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - Czochralski
  - silicon melt
  - CFD
  - ANSYS Fluent
  - design of experiments
  - surrogate model
  - physics-informed machine learning
abstract: >-
  Steady, laminar, 2D axisymmetric ANSYS Fluent simulations of the silicon melt in a
  Czochralski crucible, run over a Sobol design of crystal rotation, crucible rotation and
  hot-wall temperature. Every case uses the same 8181-node mesh and is converged to 1e-6.
  Cases that did not reach a steady solution are listed and excluded. The dataset is meant
  as reference data for surrogate and physics-informed ML models, not as a prediction of an
  industrial furnace.
